        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Merge nonce hiding subfeature into nonce]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29045</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29045"/>
        <updated>2026-02-13T12:23:50.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">I created this structure originally, but I don't like it. The implementation of the nonce attribute is complete when browsers implement it fully, so that also means nonce hiding.</p>
<p dir="auto">We can argue if we want version ranges and partial support for Firefox 31-75 and Safari 15.4-15.5 when there was no nonce hiding, but maybe that's not too interesting anymore. Happy to add it if you want me to, though.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">Data remains the same, just no sub feature anymore.<br>
Collector can more easily test this entry</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto">None open, I think.</p>]]></content>
